# shopflow - Horizon Context

Generated for Cursor by Horizon.

## Overview

This project uses Horizon for structured AI-assisted development.
All context, symbols, and specifications live in the .paradigm/ directory.


## How to Use Horizon

- Check .paradigm/specs/ for philosophy and patterns before making changes
- Reference symbols using prefixes: @feature #component ^gate !signal %state $flow
- Use the Horizon logger instead of raw console.log/print statements
- Run `horizon scan` with screenshots to map UI to code
- Check .paradigm/docs/ for command reference and troubleshooting

## Symbol System

Use these prefixes to reference project elements:

| Symbol | Name | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `@` | Feature | User-facing capabilities and functionality |
| `#` | Component | Reusable code units, UI components, or modules |
| `$` | Flow | Multi-step processes or user journeys |
| `%` | State | Global or user state conditions |
| `~` | Aspect | Cross-cutting concerns or nested properties |
| `^` | Gate | Access control points and authorization rules |
| `!` | Signal | Events, errors, and side effects |
| `?` | Idea | Free-form exploration and future possibilities |

See `.paradigm/specs/symbols.md` for complete reference.

## Horizon Logging

**IMPORTANT:** Use the Horizon logger instead of raw console.log/print.

```
// Use this pattern:
log.feature('@login').info('Starting login', { email });
log.component('#database').debug('Query executed', { duration });
log.gate('^authenticated').warn('Access denied', { userId });
log.signal('!login-success').info('User authenticated');
```

### Symbol Mapping by Directory

| Directory | Symbol | Logger Method |
|-----------|--------|---------------|
| `features/**` | `@` | `log.feature()` |
| `routes/**` | `@` | `log.feature()` |
| `api/**` | `@` | `log.feature()` |
| `components/**` | `#` | `log.component()` |
| `lib/**` | `#` | `log.component()` |
| `utils/**` | `#` | `log.component()` |
| `middleware/**` | `^` | `log.gate()` |
| `auth/**` | `^` | `log.gate()` |
| `guards/**` | `^` | `log.gate()` |
| `stores/**` | `%` | `log.state()` |
| `state/**` | `%` | `log.state()` |
| `reducers/**` | `%` | `log.state()` |
| `events/**` | `!` | `log.signal()` |
| `handlers/**` | `!` | `log.signal()` |
| `listeners/**` | `!` | `log.signal()` |
| `flows/**` | `$` | `log.flow()` |
| `sagas/**` | `$` | `log.flow()` |
| `workflows/**` | `$` | `log.flow()` |

See `.paradigm/specs/logger.md` for full specification.

## Horizon Scan

When the user says "**horizon scan**" with an image:

1. Analyze the image for UI elements
2. Cross-reference with `.paradigm/scan-index.json`
3. Return structured mapping of visual elements to code

| Mode | Use Case |
|------|----------|
| `horizon scan` | Map any image to code |
| `horizon scan ui` | Screenshot of running app |
| `horizon scan design` | Mockup - gap analysis |
| `horizon scan error` | Error screenshot |

See `.paradigm/specs/scan.md` for full protocol.

## When to Update Horizon Files

- When adding a feature, create/update the nearest .purpose file
- When adding authorization, update gate.yaml
- When exploring ideas, use ?symbol prefix
- Always update references when renaming symbols

## Conventions

- Use kebab-case for all symbol IDs (feature-name, not featureName)
- Document flows when logic spans 3+ components
- Reference related items using symbol prefixes (@ # $ % ~ ^ ! ?)
- Add descriptions to all features and gates
- Update .purpose files when changing feature behavior
- Keep gates minimal - one responsibility per gate
- Use signals for side effects, not direct state mutations
- ALWAYS use Horizon logger, NEVER raw console.log/print

## Horizon Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `horizon init` | Initialize Horizon in a project |
| `horizon sync` | Regenerate IDE instruction files |
| `horizon index` | Generate scan index |
| `horizon doctor` | Health check |
| `horizon status` | Show project status |
| `horizon watch` | Auto-sync on changes |

See `.paradigm/docs/commands.md` for full reference.

